  "body": "### Why\nFresh headed-runtime logs from 2026-08-22 showed three concrete UI regressions while the overall scheduler/observer startup remained healthy:\n\n1. an exact Galaxy S26 model candidate was briefly exposed as `selectable-item-brand_collection-10632--title`, causing one catalog cycle to fail closed before a later retry recovered;\n2. Vinted displayed the own-offer status `Anulowane`, which was stable but unsupported, so the conversation reader logged it every 500 ms for the full 20-second recognition timeout before the availability detector correctly marked the sold/removed item unavailable;\n3. the first-offer sold-state probe used Java `Pattern.UNICODE_CASE`, which Playwright Java cannot serialize to a supported JS RegExp flag.\n\n### Changes\n- accept only the known Vinted `--title` child suffix when extracting an already-proven numeric model collection ID; arbitrary suffixes still fail closed and final `brand_collection_ids[]` verification is unchanged\n- preserve unsupported visible own-offer status text in an UNKNOWN snapshot and return it immediately instead of polling the same stable label for 20 seconds\n- keep UNKNOWN fail-safe: it cannot itself trigger a follow-up offer, while downstream availability checks still run\n- remove unsupported `UNICODE_CASE` from the sold-label regex\n- add regression tests for the S26 `--title` test-id, unsupported raw status preservation, and Playwright-compatible regex flags\n\n### Safety\nNo quota, guard, idempotency, target-matching, or real-submit policy is relaxed. Exact Vinted model mode still requires exact visible label evidence and verifies the persisted collection ID end-to-end.",
